## ⚙️ Non-Negotiable Agent Rules

```
RULE 1 — NO HARDCODING
  Every value in the report must come from a file in the repository.
  Never assume a framework, owner, rule, or actor not evidenced by code.

RULE 2 — CITE EVERY CLAIM
  Every row in every table must reference the exact source file(s)
  that support it. Format: [FileName:MethodOrLineRef]

RULE 3 — STATE ABSENCES EXPLICITLY
  "No health endpoint detected" is better than silence.
  Never leave a cell blank — use "Not detected" or "Absent" with note.

RULE 4 — CONFIDENCE LEVELS ON ALL CLASSIFICATIONS
  High   = 3+ independent signals agree
  Medium = 2 signals agree, OR 1 strong unambiguous signal
  Low    = 1 weak signal OR conflicting signals
  Always explain Low confidence.

RULE 5 — DISTINGUISH ABSENCE FROM UNKNOWN
  ABSENT  = scanned and not found
  UNKNOWN = could not be determined (e.g., dynamic dispatch, generated code)

RULE 6 — NEVER EXPOSE SECRETS
  Flag credential patterns by file and type. Never print values.

RULE 7 — PRESERVE EXACT NAMES
  Use exact class names, method names, endpoint paths, error code strings,
  topic names, annotation values. Do not paraphrase or normalize.

RULE 8 — DUAL-REPO MODE
  When two repositories are provided, analyze each independently first,
  then produce cross-repo comparison sections (taxonomy, data flow, CI/CD).
  Label every repo-specific finding with [REPO-1] or [REPO-2].

RULE 9 — QUALITY GATE BEFORE OUTPUT
  Run the checklist in Phase 15 before writing the final file.
  The report is not complete until all gates pass.
```

