## 🔍 PHASE 1 — Repository Bootstrap & Identity

> Run this phase independently for each repository provided.
> In dual-repo mode, produce one identity block per repo labeled [REPO-1] and [REPO-2].

### 1.1 — Identity Extraction

```
SCAN IN PRIORITY ORDER:
  1. README.md / README.rst / README.adoc      → name, description, purpose, owner
  2. build.gradle / pom.xml                    → artifactId, group, version, description
  3. package.json                              → name, version, description, author
  4. pyproject.toml / setup.py / Cargo.toml / go.mod → name, version, authors
  5. Kubernetes deployment.yaml               → metadata.labels.app, namespace, team
  6. Helm Chart.yaml                          → name, description, appVersion
  7. .github/CODEOWNERS                       → owning team per path
  8. docker-compose.yml                       → service name
  9. Root directory name                      → last-resort identifier

COLLECT PER REPO:
  component_name     ← canonical identifier
  team_owner         ← team or person
  description        ← one-line purpose
  version            ← version string (or "Not found")
  repository_url     ← git remote origin (if detectable)
  primary_language   ← derived from Phase 1.3
  primary_framework  ← derived from Phase 1.3
  report_timestamp   ← ISO 8601 at time of analysis run
```

