### Category Decision Rules

```
IF   no vendor license files, no vendor SDK jars, no proprietary configs
→    CUSTOM

ELIF primary code base is vendor product configuration / extension
→    COTS  (e.g., Salesforce, ServiceNow, SAP)

ELIF mix of in-house code wrapping a licensed SDK / platform
→    HYBRID

ELIF purely deploying an open-source product with zero custom source
→    OPEN-SOURCE-DEPLOYMENT
```

### Sub-Category Decision Rules

```
Web Application / Service:
  @RestController OR @GetMapping OR router.get() OR [HttpGet]
  + HTTP framework in build deps
  + Exposes HTTP port in config or Dockerfile

Messaging / Event-Driven Service:
  @KafkaListener OR @RabbitListener OR consumer.subscribe()
  + No HTTP controller as PRIMARY interface

Batch / Scheduled Processing:
  @Scheduled OR @EnableBatchProcessing OR Spring Batch Step/Job config
  + Cron expression dominant pattern

Data Pipeline / ETL:
  Extract → Transform → Load pattern in service layer
  + Airflow DAGs / Prefect flows / Luigi tasks

UI / Frontend Application:
  Frontend framework in deps (React, Angular, Vue)
  + public/ or static/ directory
  + index.html entry point

Library / SDK:
  No main application entry point
  + No Dockerfile or K8s manifests
  + Published to artifact registry

CLI Tool:
  main() with argparse / cobra / click / picocli
  + No server startup code

Infrastructure / Platform:
  Primarily *.tf / CDK / Helm chart-only repo
  + No application source code
```

### Type Decision Rules

```
Microservice:
  Single focused responsibility
  + Own Dockerfile + K8s manifests
  + Stateless (no local DB, no shared filesystem)

Monolith:
  Multiple distinct domains in one deployment unit
  + Shared DB across layers
  + May contain UI

Worker / Consumer:
  Subscribes to queue/topic as PRIMARY function
  + Processes messages asynchronously

Gateway / Proxy:
  Routes, aggregates, or transforms requests
  + Contains routing rules, filters, rate-limiting
  + No direct business domain logic

Serverless Function:
  Single handler function
  + Invoked by trigger (HTTP, event, schedule)
  + No persistent server process

Sidecar:
  Injected alongside primary container
  + Handles cross-cutting concern (logging, proxy, auth)
```

