## 🌊 PART 4 — Data Flow Analysis

> Map every data movement in and out of the component — from source to sink.
> This is the most critical new section. Trace actual code paths, not assumptions.

### 4.1 — Data Source Discovery

```
SCAN FOR ALL DATA SOURCES (what feeds data INTO this component):

  HTTP Inbound:
    Scan all controller / handler classes
    For each endpoint: capture path, method, request body type, request params
    Source: [ClassName:methodName] → Request DTO class name

  Message Queue / Topic Inbound:
    @KafkaListener(topics="...") → topic name + message type
    @RabbitListener(queues="...") → queue name + message type
    @SqsListener → queue URL pattern + message type

  Database Read:
    repository.findBy*() / SELECT queries / JPA @Query
    → table/entity name, query pattern, called from which service method

  Cache Read:
    @Cacheable / redisTemplate.get() / cache.get()
    → cache name / key pattern, what data is cached

  File / Object Storage Read:
    File.read() / S3Client.getObject() / BlobServiceClient.downloadContent()
    → file path pattern or bucket/container name

  External HTTP Call (upstream):
    RestTemplate / WebClient / Axios / requests / httpx calls
    → target URL pattern, response type

  Scheduled Data Injection:
    @Scheduled method that reads data → what it reads, from where

  Environment / Config Data:
    @Value / process.env / os.environ / config.get()
    → config key names (not values), source file
```

### 4.2 — Data Sink Discovery

```
SCAN FOR ALL DATA SINKS (where data LEAVES this component):

  HTTP Response:
    Return type of each controller method → response body DTO class
    HTTP status codes set explicitly

  Message Queue / Topic Outbound:
    KafkaTemplate.send() → topic name, message type
    RabbitTemplate.convertAndSend() → exchange/queue, message type
    SqsClient.sendMessage() → queue URL pattern, message type

  Database Write:
    repository.save() / INSERT / UPDATE queries
    → table/entity name, written by which service method

  Cache Write:
    @CachePut / @CacheEvict / redisTemplate.set()
    → cache name / key pattern, TTL if specified

  File / Object Storage Write:
    File.write() / S3Client.putObject() / BlobServiceClient.uploadContent()
    → path pattern or bucket/container name

  External HTTP Call (fire-and-forget / downstream notification):
    POST/PUT to external service with no response dependency

  Event / Webhook Publish:
    ApplicationEventPublisher.publishEvent()
    → event class name

  Log Output:
    Structured logging sinks (Splunk, ELK, CloudWatch)
    → derived from logback/log4j appender config or logging dependency
```

