## ⚠️ PART 13 — Gap Analysis

### 13.1 — Gap Detection Rules by Category

```
RUN ALL CATEGORIES. For each gap found, assign a G-ID (G-001, G-002, ...).

CAT-1: TEST COVERAGE GAPS
  ⛔ UC has zero test coverage (any type)
  ⚠️ UC has unit tests only — no integration or BDD
  ⚠️ Error path has no test scenario covering it
  ⚠️ Validator class has no test class

CAT-2: DOCUMENTATION GAPS
  ⛔ HTTP endpoint has no Javadoc/docstring AND no OpenAPI annotation
  ⛔ No OpenAPI/Swagger spec for externally-consumed HTTP service
  ⚠️ README absent or fewer than 100 words
  ⚠️ Error code exists in source but has no i18n message
  ⚠️ Request/response DTO has no field-level documentation

CAT-3: ERROR HANDLING GAPS
  ⛔ Exception thrown in service not caught by @ControllerAdvice
  ⛔ Catch block that swallows exception silently
  ⚠️ Error code constant defined but never used in any code path
  ⚠️ Error code used in code but no matching constant (magic string)
  ⚠️ No standardized error response body across endpoints

CAT-4: BUSINESS RULE GAPS
  ⛔ TODO / FIXME comment inside validator or service business logic
  ⛔ Commented-out validation logic (security or compliance rule)
  ⚠️ Partial rule implementation (method stub or empty body)
  ⚠️ Error code in messages.properties not triggered by any code path
  ⚠️ Rule referenced in test fixture not enforced in source code

CAT-5: DATA FLOW GAPS
  ⛔ Data source consumed but no validation / sanitization before use
  ⛔ External HTTP call with no timeout / circuit breaker configuration
  ⚠️ Response DTO leaks internal field names or stack traces
  ⚠️ Cache used but no TTL or eviction policy found in config
  ⚠️ Message consumer with no dead-letter queue configuration

CAT-6: OBSERVABILITY GAPS
  ⛔ HTTP endpoint with no request/response logging
  ⛔ Error path with no log statement (silent failure)
  ⚠️ No correlation / trace ID propagation in request handling
  ⚠️ Business rule violation not emitted as metric or audit log
  ⚠️ Health endpoint absent for container-deployed service

CAT-7: CI/CD PIPELINE GAPS
  ⛔ No CI/CD pipeline configuration found
  ⛔ Pipeline has no test execution step
  ⛔ Pipeline deploys to production with no manual gate
  ⚠️ No dependency vulnerability scan in pipeline
  ⚠️ No code coverage enforcement (threshold) in pipeline
  ⚠️ Docker image built but not scanned for vulnerabilities
  ⚠️ No artifact signing or SBOM generation

CAT-8: TRACEABILITY GAPS
  ⛔ Feature file test has no matching source implementation
  ⚠️ Validator class exists but is not called from any entry point
  ⚠️ Requirement implied by test but no code enforces it
  ⚠️ Multiple UCs share a validator with no discriminator logic

SEVERITY ASSIGNMENT:
  CRITICAL = Production failure risk, security risk, or compliance risk
  HIGH     = Reliability risk or significant functional gap
  MEDIUM   = Quality or maintainability risk
  LOW      = Minor improvement opportunity
```

